     1	# Workspace-local runtime provisioning
     2	
     3	Boring UI provisions runtime resources inside the selected workspace. Opening a
     4	workspace through the app shell or `npx @hachej/boring-ui-cli` is intended to be
     5	zero setup: generated skills, package CLIs, SDKs, and starter files appear under
     6	that workspace before the agent runtime is ready.
     7	
     8	## Generated layout
     9	
    10	All generated state lives under:
    11	
    12	```text
    13	$BORING_AGENT_WORKSPACE_ROOT/.boring-agent/
    14	├── .gitignore
    15	├── skills/          # generated mirror of plugin skills
    16	├── node/            # npm prefix for runtime Node CLIs
    17	├── venv/            # Python virtualenv for runtime Python CLIs/SDKs
    18	├── sdk/             # staged local SDK/package sources (sdk/uv = workspace-local uv)
    19	├── cache/           # npm/uv/pip caches
    20	└── tmp/             # staged venvs, tarballs, temp files
    21	```
    22	
    23	Provisioning skip state is tracked via ownership markers and fingerprints stored
    24	alongside managed directories (see `runtimeLayout.ts`), not a separate
    25	`fingerprints/` directory.
    26	
    27	`.boring-agent` is generated and disposable. Do not hand-edit it; delete it to
    28	force a full local reprovision. The directory writes its own `.gitignore` and
    29	should not be committed.
    30	
    31	User-authored skills still belong in `.agents/skills`. Plugin-provided skills
    32	are copied into `.boring-agent/skills/<plugin-id>/<skill-name>` so normal
    33	workspace reads can inspect them. Provisioning never overwrites `.agents/skills`.
    34	
    35	## When provisioning runs
    36	
    37	Provisioning is synchronous and idempotent:
    38	
    39	- workspace/app load runs provisioning before declaring the agent runtime ready;
    40	- CLI project mode provisions the selected project workspace;
    41	- CLI workspaces/global mode provisions the saved selected workspace, not the
    42	  registry directory or home directory;
    43	- `POST /api/v1/agent/reload` reruns provisioning, recopies edited skills,
    44	  reseeds missing files, and refreshes prompt/resources;
    45	- runtime installs are skipped when fingerprints and expected outputs still
    46	  match.
    47	
    48	Set `provisionWorkspace: false` to opt out. In that mode Boring UI does not write
    49	`.boring-agent` and no package source copies or installs run.
    50	
    51	There is no provisioning job/status/doctor endpoint in this first pass. Failures
    52	surface synchronously with stable `PROVISIONING_*` error codes and structured
    53	logs. Concurrent first-load/reload calls are not locked yet; avoid intentionally
    54	starting multiple provisioning runs for the same workspace at once.
    55	
    56	## Package authoring shape
    57	
    58	Package metadata uses the existing public namespaces only:
    59	
    60	```jsonc
    61	{
    62	  "name": "@example/macro",
    63	  "pi": {
    64	    "skills": ["src/server/workspace-template/.agents/skills/macro-transform"],
    65	    "systemPrompt": "Use bm for macro transforms.",
    66	    "packages": ["npm:pi-web-access"],
    67	    "extensions": []
    68	  },
    69	  "boring": {
    70	    "front": "src/front/index.tsx",
    71	    "server": "src/server/index.ts"
    72	  }
    73	}
    74	```
    75	
    76	- `pi.skills` are mirrored into `.boring-agent/skills`.
    77	- `pi.systemPrompt`, `pi.packages`, `pi.extensions`, and prompts remain Pi
    78	  resources and flow through the Pi loader/prompt builder.
    79	- `boring.front` discovers UI contributions.
    80	- `boring.server` discovers trusted server code.
    81	
    82	There is no third public manifest namespace for provisioning. Future
    83	workspace-installed plugin declarations are deferred and are not first-pass
    84	behavior.
    85	
    86	## Trusted server provisioning
    87	
    88	Trusted `boring.server` code can declare runtime provisioning for SDKs,
    89	templates, and environment variables:
    90	
    91	```ts
    92	import { defineServerPlugin } from "@hachej/boring-workspace/server"
    93	
    94	export default defineServerPlugin({
    95	  id: "boring-macro",
    96	  provisioning: {
    97	    python: [{
    98	      id: "macro-sdk",
    99	      packageName: "boring-macro-sdk",
   100	      projectFile: "src/server/sdk/pyproject.toml",
   101	      expectedBins: ["bm"],
   102	      env: { BORING_MACRO_API_URL: "http://localhost:3000/api/macro" },
   103	    }],
   104	    templateDirs: [{
   105	      id: "macro-template",
   106	      path: "src/server/workspace-template",
   107	    }],
   108	  },
   109	  routes(app) {
   110	    // Macro HTTP/API integration.
   111	  },
   112	  agentTools: [
   113	    // Only trusted server-stateful tools that need DB/API clients/auth.
   114	  ],
   115	})
   116	```
   117	
   118	After provisioning, a macro-style workspace has:
   119	
   120	```text
   121	.boring-agent/skills/boring-macro/macro-transform/SKILL.md
   122	.boring-agent/venv/bin/bm
   123	.deck/intro.md                         # seeded only if missing
   124	transforms/custom/.gitkeep             # seeded only if missing
   125	```
   126	
   127	The harness PATH includes `.boring-agent/venv/bin`, and runtime command env
   128	includes `BORING_MACRO_API_URL`. Existing user files are preserved; templates
   129	copy only missing files.
   130	
   131	Regular portable package/runtime plugins should prefer `pi.extensions` or future
   132	portable sandbox-tool declarations instead of `boring.server.agentTools`.
   133	
   134	## Runtime-mode consistency
   135	
   136	`direct`, `local`/bwrap, and `vercel-sandbox` use the same provisioning engine and
   137	same runtime layout. Mode adapters own transport details:
   138	
   139	- direct/local can use local package paths directly;
   140	- Vercel-like adapters turn path-invisible local packages into workspace-visible
   141	  artifact sources;
   142	- adapters choose cache roots and enforce path-safety for workspace file writes.
   143	
   144	The shared provisioning engine never calls Vercel APIs, `npm pack`, upload APIs,
   145	or cloud credentials directly.
   146	
   147	## Verification commands
   148	
   149	Useful smoke/unit checks:
   150	
   151	```bash
   152	pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-cli exec vitest run src/__tests__/runtimeProvisioning.test.ts
   153	pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-workspace exec vitest run src/app/server/__tests__/macroRuntimeProvisioning.test.ts
   154	pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-workspace exec vitest run src/server/__tests__/createWorkspaceAgentServer.test.ts --testNamePattern "runtime provisioning reload"
   155	pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-sandbox exec vitest run src/providers/vercel-sandbox/__tests__/provisioningAdapter.test.ts
   156	pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-agent exec vitest run src/server/workspace/provisioning/__tests__
   157	```

