The trust boundary is worse than runtime tampering: workspace-controlled plugin metadata can point `boring.server` at agent-written JavaScript, and reload/open imports it into the unsandboxed host process. I’m treating that as the sole FATAL trust finding and separating it from persistent prompt/skill influence.
