+## Finding 27 — Two agent types conflict instead of rotating generations
+
+Severity: MINOR
+
+Attack area: concurrency / availability.
+
+Exact failing sequence:
+
+1. Agent type A acquires a workspace+placement environment with fingerprint A.
+2. Agent type B resolves the same workspace+placement with fingerprint B.
+3. The lease manager detects mismatch.
+4. It immediately throws instead of queuing a generation swap or provisioning a
+   separate immutable generation.
+5. B remains unavailable while A retains any reference.
